{
  "id": "ss.base.cairn",
  "name": "Salt cairn",
  "description": "Three slabs of the pan's salt plate stacked by the north-west road, drawn the way the pan's own plates are (`ss.terrain.saltplate`), salt crusted white along their edges and cracked, a chip fallen at the foot, with a stake bound into them and a frayed strip of cold cloth flapping on it (`flutter`): hoisted along the stake, cut into lengths so ripples run out along it to its tails, each fold darkening as it passes. The canvas is wider than the slabs so the tails have room to whip. In feelers this is the way out to the Salt Pan.",
  "tags": ["base"],
  "size": [40, 60],
